## Behind the returns desk

::bg{location="library_back_room" time="afternoon"}
::auto{character="ines" anchor="right" action="slideInRight"}
::set{run.seen.ines = run.day}
@ines{emotion="happy"}: You remembered! Nobody remembers Wednesdays.
@narrator: On the desk: a flat parcel in brown paper, already opened, the sheets inside the colour of weak tea.
@ines: Kozo. I ordered extra. Don't tell the council.
::set{run.lantern.paper = true}
@ines{emotion="shy"}: I could — show you how to fold the corners. So they don't tear on the frame. If you want.

<branch id="fold" prompt="She has already rolled up her sleeves.">
  <choice id="together" label="“Show me.”">
    ::set{run.aff.ines += 2}
    @narrator: Her hands are cold and quick. She folds; you copy; she refolds yours without comment, and then, eventually, doesn't have to.
    @ines{emotion="happy"}: There. You have lantern hands now.
  </choice>
  <choice id="self" label="“I'll manage, thanks.”">
    @ines{emotion="neutral"}: Of course. Mind the corners.
  </choice>
</branch>

::auto{character="ines" action="fadeOut"}
